# BOT DEE rename (from FloqAi / floqai.*)

Resume: `@botdee$` / `@floqai-page$`.

Patron product name is **BOT DEE** (protected brand). This note records how the rename was done so later agents do not reintroduce `floqai.html` or treat `floqAi` as the live catalog key.

## Phase A — page URL (s3.2.74 → s3.2.75) — DONE

| Step | What |
|---|---|
| A1 | Canonical chat page became `botdee.html` (was `floqai.html`). Nav `intentSearchHome()`, Search tile, feature `route`, help links, intent cards all target `./botdee.html`. |
| A2 | s3.2.74 briefly kept `floqai.html` + `floqai-search.html` as **redirect stubs** to `botdee.html`. |
| A3 | s3.2.75 **deleted** both stubs (404, no redirect). Owner decision: do not keep a FloqAi URL. |
| A4 | Patron-facing copy already said BOT DEE (chrome / help packs). Floating agent speech fixed to `Hi, I am BOT DEE` (`botdee-search.js`). Auth gate no longer lists `floqai-search.html` as public. |

## Phase B — technical ids (s3.2.76) — DONE

Same pattern as floqCast ← `supRstar` (one-release dual-read).

### Catalog / Features & Services

| Before | After | Dual-read |
|---|---|---|
| `featureServices/floqAi` | `featureServices/botDee` | `canonicalizeFeatureKey("floqAi") → "botDee"`; `loadFeature` falls back to legacy `floqAi` doc; `seedFeatureServices` copies flags from `floqAi` when creating `botDee` |
| `data-feature-key="floqAi"` / `data-floqr-feature="floqAi"` | `botDee` | Alias still accepted via canonicalize |
| Chrome pack key `floqAi` | `botDee` | `data-floqr-chrome-icon` dual-read: `floqAi` → `botDee` assets |

