### i18n / help ids

Chrome keys: `floqai.*` / `page.floqai.*` / `cat.floqai*` / `template.floqai*` → `botdee.*` / `page.botdee.*` / `cat.botdee*` / `template.botdee*` (all 11 langs, same change).

Help ids: `help-floqai-page` → `help-botdee-page`; `help-floqai-template-search` → `help-botdee-template-search`; `floqai-ask-floqr` → `botdee-ask-floqr`; `help-floqai-audience-sections` → `help-botdee-audience-sections`.

### DOM / CSS

Ids such as `categoryFloqAi*` / `floqAiAgent` / `floqAiSearchPanel` → `categoryBotDee*` / `botDeeAgent` / `botDeeSearchPanel`. CSS class prefix `.floqai-` → `.botdee-` (pages already carried many `botdee-*` classes).

### Storage note

Firestore collection `floqAiAccessThrottle` (and related audit wording) may still exist historically; new writes use `botDeeAccessThrottle` when the access callable was updated. Prefer dual-read on throttle if both can appear during the alias window.

## Do not

- Do not recreate `floqai.html` or a redirect page.
- Do not show **FloqAi** in patron/admin UI chrome (label is **BOT DEE**).
- Do not invent a second chat page — only `botdee.html`.
- Do not drop `canonicalizeFeatureKey("floqAi")` until Master Admin has seeded `featureServices/botDee` and beta `features.botDee` maps are backfilled / dual-read proven.

